3. What is Event Bubbling? And how does it work?
Event Bubbling is when an event occurs on an element, it first happens on that element and then gradually bubbles up to its parent elements.

4.What is Event Delegation in JavaScript? Why is it useful?

Event Delegation is attaching a single event listener to a parent element and using the event object to identify which child element triggered the event.
5.What is the difference between preventDefault() and stopPropagation() methods?
`preventDefault()`  stops the browser’s default action
`stopPropagation()`  stops event bubbling/capturing

